{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1536","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Omkar and Bad Story"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Omkar has received a message from Anton saying \"Your story for problem A is confusing. Just make a formal statement.\" Because of this, Omkar gives you an array $$$a = [a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n]$$$ of $$$n$$$ distinct integers. An array $$$b = [b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_k]$$$ is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if for any two distinct elements $$$b_i, b_j$$$ of $$$b$$$, $$$|b_i-b_j|$$$ appears in $$$b$$$ at least once. In addition, all elements in $$$b$$$ must be distinct. Can you add several (maybe, $$$0$$$) integers to $$$a$$$ to create a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array $$$b$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"of size at most $$$300$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"? If $$$a$$$ is already "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", you don't have to add any elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, array $$$[3, 6, 9]$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as $$$|6-3|=|9-6| = 3$$$, which appears in the array, and $$$|9-3| = 6$$$, which appears in the array, while array $$$[4, 2, 0, 6, 9]$$$ is not "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as $$$|9-4| = 5$$$ is not present in the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$, $$$|x-y| = x-y$$$ if $$$x \\gt y$$$ and $$$|x-y| = y-x$$$ otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 50$$$), the number of test cases. Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 100$$$) — the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\cdots, a_n$$$ ($$$-100 \\leq a_i \\leq 100$$$) — the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output one line containing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if Omkar can create a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array $$$b$$$ by adding elements to $$$a$$$ and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise. The case of each letter does not matter, so "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will also be accepted."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the first line is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", output a second line containing a single integer $$$k$$$ ($$$n \\leq k \\leq 300$$$). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then output one line containing $$$k$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\cdots, b_k$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\leq b_i \\leq 10^9$$$), the elements of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array $$$b$$$. $$$b_1, b_2, \\cdots, b_k$$$ can be in any order. For each $$$a_i$$$ in $$$a$$$, $$$a_i$$$ must appear at least once in $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proved that if Omkar can create such an array $$$b$$$, then he can also do so in a way that satisfies the above constraints."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If multiple solutions exist, you can print any. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n3 0 9\n2\n3 4\n5\n-7 3 13 -2 8\n4\n4 8 12 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nyes\n4\n6 0 3 9\nyEs\n5\n5 3 1 2 4\nNO\nYes\n6\n8 12 6 2 4 10\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the first case, you can add integers to $$$a$$$ to receive the array $$$b = [6, 0, 3, 9]$$$. Note that $$$|6-3| = |9-6| = |3-0| = 3$$$ and $$$3$$$ is in $$$b$$$, $$$|6-0| = |9-3| = 6$$$ and $$$6$$$ is in $$$b$$$, and $$$|9-0| = 9$$$ is in $$$b$$$, so $$$b$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second case, you can add integers to $$$a$$$ to receive the array $$$b = [5, 3, 1, 2, 4]$$$. We have that $$$|2-1| = |3-2| = |4-3| = |5-4| = 1$$$ is in $$$b$$$, $$$|3-1| = |4-2| = |5-3| = 2$$$ is in $$$b$$$, $$$|4-1| = |5-2| = 3$$$ is in $$$b$$$, and $$$|5-1| = 4$$$ is in $$$b$$$, so $$$b$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the fourth case, you can add integers to $$$a$$$ to receive the array $$$b = [8, 12, 6, 2, 4, 10]$$$. We have that $$$|4-2| = |6-4| = |8-6| = |10-8| = |12-10| = 2$$$ is in $$$b$$$, $$$|6-2| = |8-4| = |10-6| = |12-8| = 4$$$ is in $$$b$$$, $$$|8-2| = |10-4| = |12-6| = 6$$$ is in $$$b$$$, $$$|10-2| = |12-4| = 8$$$ is in $$$b$$$, and $$$|12-2| = 10$$$ is in $$$b$$$, so $$$b$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proven that for all other test cases it is impossible to create a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1536A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1536/problem/A"}